<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan sells 8.8 bln rupees bonds.</title>
<headline>Pakistan sells 8.8 bln rupees bonds.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan said it had accepted 8.8 billion rupees in an open market operation in short-term federal bonds on Saturday.</p>
<p>		    Offered	  Accepted	 Max cut-off</p>
<p>Outright sales  7.70 bln	  7.70 bln     16.99 pct/yr</p>
<p>One-week repo   0.15 bln	  0.15 bln     14.00 pct/yr</p>
<p>One-month repo  0.95 bln	  0.95 bln     15.00 pct/yr</p>
<p>Total	     8.80 bln	  8.80 bln     15.00 pct/yr</p>
<p>-- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
